WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.140
Diana of Themyscira isn't afraid to speak
truth to power... or, failing that, to just

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.340
kick power's ass.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.571
WarnerMedia unveiled new footage from the
upcoming Wonder Woman 1984 at their HBO Max

00:00:11.571 --> 00:00:16.260
presentation this week, and it features Gal
Gadot's Diana engaged in a brawl in an unlikely

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.390
place: inside the White House.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.020
The promotion machine for the sequel to the
2017 smash hit Wonder Woman is finally starting

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.800
to kick into gear, and while it doesn't look
like the new footage is going to be released

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.120
online, we have a detailed breakdown thanks
to the folks at IGN.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.579
The footage heavily features Chris Pine's
Steve Trevor, whom you may remember appeared

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.000
to be quite dead at the conclusion of the
first film.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.379
It's unclear how he'll return, especially
considering the nearly four-decade time jump

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:46.101
between the two movies; Diana may be a virtually
ageless quasi-goddess, but when it comes to

00:00:46.101 --> 00:00:50.269
Trevor, the filmmakers will have some pretty
heavy narrative lifting to do in explaining

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:53.170
his apparent resurrection and failure to age.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:57.199
Perhaps they'll steal a page from the classic
'70s and '80s Wonder Woman television series

00:00:57.199 --> 00:01:01.989
— when it jumped time periods from the '40s
to the '70s, the presence of Trevor, portrayed

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:06.180
by the same actor, was hand-waved with the
explanation that '70s Trevor was actually

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.700
the original guy's son... who looked identical
to his father, right down to the haircut.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.740
Sure, why not?

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.251
At any rate, the new footage opens with a
shot of Trevor and Diana strolling along by

00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:20.610
the Washington Monument, with Diana wearing
the type of flowy, white dress that one might

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:24.880
expect to see on Themyscira, but not necessarily
in Washington, D.C.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.320
In voiceover, she says the line of dialogue,
"I can almost see it, like a beautiful dream,"

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.900
as she caresses Steve's face.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:35.420
In the next scene, Trevor and Diana are seen
under attack from gun-wielding assailants

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.820
in the halls of the White House, which doesn't
sound like a beautiful dream at all.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.960
Like we said, we don't actually have access
to this footage — but it may look a little

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.780
something like the last time a superhero took
on the White House in the second X-Men movie.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.900
It might also look a little bit like this.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.300
Just use your imagination.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.500
In the actual footage, Diana is wearing that
crazy new armor that was teased in a promotional

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.940
one-sheet back in June, and she has her hands
full protecting Trevor from incoming gunfire

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.400
while taking down baddies.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.530
The clip briefly moves to slow motion as Diana
snatches away an attacker's gun and deftly

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:09.969
unloads it, then she brings her lasso into
play, roping guys in and pulling them towards

00:02:09.969 --> 00:02:13.719
her so she can deliver finishing blows in
a maneuver that would make Mortal Kombat's

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.720
Scorpion proud.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.060
“Get over here!"

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.840
The clip ends as Diana uses her lasso to deflect
a bolt of energy from an unseen opponent.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.420
The footage reveals that Diana will be facing
down some powerful enemies, both in terms

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.620
of political power and... well, freaky energy
bolts.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:36.160
Unfortunately, it doesn't clue us in as to
the deal with Trevor, so we'll just go ahead

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.020
and guess that he somehow survived his plane
blowing up at a high altitude, then went on

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.880
to invent the most amazing anti-wrinkle cream
the world has ever seen.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.190
So far, only a precious few people have gotten
to actually see this footage from the movie,

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.660
as no trailer for the sequel has yet been
released.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:54.800
However, thanks to director Patty Jenkins
spilling the beans, we now know when that

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.440
will happen: on December 8, at the Comic-Con
Experience in São Paulo, Brazil.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:02.940
The flick's panel will close out the event,
which will be live-streamed via its official

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:03.500
Twitter page.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.820
Although it hasn't been officially confirmed,
it's assumed that the CCXP spot will drop

00:03:07.829 --> 00:03:12.329
online shortly thereafter; fans have been
waiting a long time, and principal photography

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.760
on the film wrapped about a year ago, so we
can probably expect a pretty beefy first trailer.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:19.240
"What are you?"

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.220
"You'll soon find out!"

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.540
Hopefully, a bit of the mystery surrounding
the plot of Wonder Woman 1984 will be cleared

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:27.260
up when that trailer drops next month.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.569
The first film's director Patty Jenkins also
helmed this installment, working from a script

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:35.720
she co-wrote with Shang-Chi and the Legend
of the Ten Rings scribe Dave Callaham and

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.280
comics writer Geoff Johns.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.480
In addition to Gal Gadot and Chris Pine, the
cast includes Connie Nielsen and Robin Wright,

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.580
reprising their roles as Hippolyta and Antiope,
respectively.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:50.299
Joining Wonder Woman newcomers Pedro Pascal
as Maxwell Lord and Kristen Wiig as Barbara

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:55.140
Minerva — AKA Cheetah — are Gabriella
Wilde, Ravi Patel, and Natasha Rothwell.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.440
The movie hits the big screen on June 5, 2020.

